{"body": "This PR introduces a separate executor service for HiveTablesTest$testConcurrentFastAppends.\nRight now, the test depends on the size of the worker pool. If the size is less 3, the test will not complete as the same worker pool is used in SnapshotUpdate$apply (because manifest lists are now enabled and it requires at least one thread).\nThe executor service does not use a custom ThreadFactory. Threads will be non-daemon, but shouldn't be a problem as the result is wrapped into MoreExecutors.getExitingExecutorService.", "date": "2019-01-07T21:32:45Z", "hash": "sha256:cb949ef22768791c9e62", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#67", "meta": {"additions": 8, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-01-07T22:04:54Z", "comments": 1, "deletions": 2, "draft": false, "files": ["hive/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/hive/HiveTablesTest.java"], "merged_at": "2019-01-07T22:04:54Z", "merged_by": "rdblue", "n_files": 1, "number": 67, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2019-01-08T08:02:45Z"}, "people": ["aokolnychyi"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Use a separate executor service for the concurrent Hive test", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/67"}
