{"body": "This is safe because schema updates can always read older data. If a\ntransaction includes a write followed by a schema update, the new schema\ncan read the data that was just written. Also, writers are allowed to\nwrite with older schemas because the current schema can read any file\nwritten with an older schema. If a transaction includes a schema update\nfollowed by a write, using either the original schema or the new schema\nwill work.", "date": "2019-01-10T23:20:25Z", "hash": "sha256:716d4b14fbce450b4550", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#70", "meta": {"additions": 16, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-01-14T19:01:25Z", "comments": 0, "deletions": 1, "draft": false, "files": ["api/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/Transaction.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/BaseTransaction.java"], "merged_at": "2019-01-14T19:01:25Z", "merged_by": "rdblue", "n_files": 2, "number": 70, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2019-01-14T18:59:53Z", "by": "Parth-Brahmbhatt", "state": "APPROVED"}], "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2019-01-14T19:01:25Z"}, "people": ["rdblue"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Allow schema updates in transactions.", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/70"}
