{"body": "FilteredManifest only ran filters if there was a row filter AND a\npartition filter, but it should run filteres if there is a row filter OR\na partition filter.\nBecause a filter may be null, this also updates the functions that\ncreate evaluators to create an evaluator for alwaysTrue when the\nexpression is null.", "date": "2019-01-10T23:20:58Z", "hash": "sha256:c785a4035f57af38d3d3", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#72", "meta": {"additions": 119, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-01-14T18:54:58Z", "comments": 3, "deletions": 8, "draft": false, "files": ["core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/FilteredManifest.java", "core/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/TestFilterFiles.java"], "merged_at": "2019-01-14T18:54:58Z", "merged_by": "rdblue", "n_files": 2, "number": 72, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2019-01-14T18:51:26Z", "by": "Parth-Brahmbhatt", "state": "APPROVED"}], "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2019-01-14T18:54:58Z"}, "people": ["rdblue"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Fix filtering manifests in unpartitioned tables.", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/72"}
